Oh yeah, copy is still queen. You just haven;t tested it yet. 

On YouTube, the title of your video can drive vastly different results. Changing the title alone has yielded a $50 range between CPAs in past tests I've run for my day job. What does this mean? 
Well, it truly varies by channel but at least on YouTube, you should not title your video arbitrarily. At the very least, give it a readable title. At best, figure out the content your audience resonates with and speak to them that way. Keep an eye out for trends and patterns that really only work for Organic. And figure out ways to hack small changes that convert organic insights into paid wins.

Here are some title formulas I've tested in the past. I won't say which worked best, as it varies by category but give 'em a test and see what you discover.
* **Comparison: "Why X is better than Y"
* **Confirmation:** (Yes, we have [xyz])
* **Tag along:** ([verb] [xyz] with me)
* **1P Creator:** (i.e., Everything I Tried from [xyz]) try this despite posting from the Brand handle
* **3P Creator:** (@[creator handle]'s [adjective] [subject/brand/action]) try this despite their handle or following on the ad platform
* **Explainer Question:** (What is/are [product/behavior/service]?)
* **Negative Question:** (What's wrong with [product/behavior/service]?)
* **Qualifier Question: (What makes [xyz] a [brand/stan name, etc.]?) 
* **Reason: "Why we [verb] [action]"
* **One-of-a-kind claim:** ([Action/Verb] these [adjective, i.e. unique, exclusive] [product/service])
* **Seasonality:** ([xyz] is bank in stock/season)
* **How it works:** (How does [xyz] work?)
* **Generic mission: fight / hate food waste
* **Product stan:** (Why we love [xyz], This is our favorite [xyz])
* **Quiz:** (Can you guess [xyz])
* **Curiosity tease:** (The secret behind [xyz], The simplest reason to try [xyz])
